# env

Bionic toolchain for AGY: a self-contained Android prefix at `$PREFIX` under
the installed app's private `files/usr` directory, a package manager (`pkg`),
and a path-rewrite helper. Paths and app id are resolved at install/runtime;
no fixed `dev.continuum.antigravity` path is required. No root, no proot.

```
env/bootstrap/   Termux bootstrap archive + prefix patch
env/overlay/     files copied verbatim into $PREFIX (etc, bin/rish, ...)
env/pkg/         pkg + its shell libraries
env/dist/env/    packaged assets consumed by EnvInstaller
env/tests/       offline selftest / invariant / e3 checks
```

## Termux prefix rewriting

The Termux bootstrap and its packages can contain legacy
`/data/data/<application-id>/files/usr` or user-scoped
`/data/user/<user-id>/<application-id>/files/usr` paths in shebangs, helper
bodies (`gzexe` tmpdir, dpkg `.list`, `*-config`) and absolute symlinks. The
active prefix is app-private and varies by application id and Android user.

Two layers handle these paths:

1. **Install time.** `TermuxShebangRewriter`, `TermuxPrefixRewriter` and
   `TermuxSymlinkFixer` repoint recognized prefixes to the active `$PREFIX`.
   Text rewrites cover `$PREFIX/{bin,libexec,etc,share,var}`; absolute prefix
   symlinks are fixed separately. `pkg install` applies the same dynamic text
   rewrite to each extracted package via `rewrite_prefix` in `pkg/lib/util.sh`.
2. **After third-party installers.** `pip`, `npm` and friends write console
   scripts that bake in the Termux interpreter path. Run the shipped helper:

```sh
agy-fix-paths                 # rewrite the whole prefix
agy-fix-paths ~/site/bin      # only these files/dirs
agy-fix-paths ./venv/bin/*    # globs expanded by the shell
```

`agy-fix-paths` prints the number of files rewritten. It is idempotent (files
already using `$PREFIX` are left byte-identical) and skips binaries and
symlinks. It lives at `env/overlay/bin/agy-fix-paths` and is installed to
`$PREFIX/bin/agy-fix-paths`.
